1. THE THREE FORMS OF THE GROWING WALL ON A STREAM (H = 1/400 per interval; rows one per interval; 1 + z = the arrival spacing)
  wall with the age  : distance 100 Links, first arrival at tick 214, spacing 1.000 (1 + z), the formula's 1.000
  wall with the age  : distance 300 Links, first arrival at tick 1052, spacing 1.000 (1 + z), the formula's 1.000
  wall with the birth: distance 100 Links, first arrival at tick 172, spacing 1.429 (1 + z), the formula's 1.430
  wall with the birth: distance 300 Links, first arrival at tick 515, spacing 2.291 (1 + z), the formula's 2.289
  wall with the tick : distance 100 Links, first arrival at tick 214, spacing 1.539 (1 + z), the formula's 1.537
  wall with the tick : distance 300 Links, first arrival at tick 1052, spacing 3.639 (1 + z), the formula's 3.629
  the age wall gives every row the same flight and no redshift; the birth wall gives z = H d / c_0, the tick wall 1 + z = a(t_r) / a(t_e) = e^(H d / c_0), the Milne form z = tau / (1 / H + t_r - tau)

2. THE 24 THROWN STARS OF coasting_none AT REST UNDER THE GROWING TICK WALL: z = tau / (T - tau)
  T = 440.0: rms 0.0044, worst +0.0082 (s_pz3); the README's grain 0.003, its fit's rms 0.0019
  T = 428.8: rms 0.0076, worst -0.0160 (s_mz4); the README's grain 0.003, its fit's rms 0.0019
  the birth wall's form z = H tau at the same H: rms 0.0808, worst +0.1553: refuted by the far stars
  the thrown coasting star's own relation: z = v / c and tau = v (T - tau) / c give z = tau / (T - tau), the same Milne form: the two models coincide in z(tau)

3. SEELIGER IN A PERIODIC WORLD (an eternal source of q rows per interval, a periodic cube of extent 301; the presence at 10 Links, summed over the periodic images the light has reached)
  static      , after   1000 intervals: the light's reach     582 Links, images     27, presence 0.000809 (units of q dwell)
  static      , after   3000 intervals: the light's reach    1745 Links, images    799, presence 0.000851 (units of q dwell)
  static      , after  10000 intervals: the light's reach    5818 Links, images  30307, presence 0.001001 (units of q dwell)
  growing wall, after   1000 intervals: the light's reach     292 Links, images      2, presence 0.000763 (units of q dwell)
  growing wall, after   3000 intervals: the light's reach     498 Links, images     19, presence 0.000765 (units of q dwell)
  growing wall, after  10000 intervals: the light's reach     758 Links, images     81, presence 0.000765 (units of q dwell)
  static: the images within reach grow as (2 c_0 t / L)^3 and their fluxes 1 / d^2 sum to about 4 pi c_0 t / L^3 beyond the first: the presence grows without bound, linearly in t (Seeliger);
  growing wall: the reach saturates at (c_0 / H) ln(1 + H t) and each image's flux is cut off by e^(-H d / c_0) at the Hubble length c_0 / H = 233 Links: the sum converges (the nearest image and a tail)
